/-- Kernel pin on the HAT side: `hatP 4` is the tale-1 engine's `p_4`.  Rendered by
`gen_hat_lean.hatP_pin_lines`, the same function `Zeta2HatCheck.lean` uses for n ≤ 3. -/
theorem hatP_engine : hatP 4 = (-32687805874306297157279894551933452315199490169511109524526347752919671934527515616709657991323 / 2671126941122562502944000 : ℚ) := by
